body:
`formatPercent` treats values exactly equal to 1 or -1 as “whole-number percent”, so 1 renders as `1%` instead of the common decimal convention `100%`. Consider treating `|value| <= 1` as decimal input (or otherwise disambiguate) so 1 maps to 100%.
```suggestion
  // If absolute value is <= 1, treat as decimal (e.g. 0.8 → 80%, 1 → 100%)
  const displayValue = Math.abs(value) <= 1 ? value * 100 : value;
```
